# YAML

- Follow the owning schema, application, and declared YAML version. Kubernetes, GitHub Actions, Compose, and other dialects impose different semantics.
- Preserve indentation, document separators, quoting, anchors, key order, and scalar style according to repository convention and consumer behavior.
- Quote ambiguous scalars when the consumer or YAML version may reinterpret them; do not assume YAML 1.2 support without evidence.
- Validate changed data with its owning schema or tool. Use the configured formatter or linter rather than assuming Prettier.
- Do not apply class, interface, or dependency-injection guidance, and do not hand-edit generated YAML unless the approved workflow requires it.
